# T6b. A capture keeps its type: n is a size_t formal of the host, and the node's field n is a
# size_t cell. addBig carries 2^32, addSmall 2^32 - 1; addN tells them apart: 101 and 2.
# The base translator refused ("a callable merge needs a walkable body"). Mutant: the capture
# made an int cell -- 2^32 is 0 there, addBig: 1 is 2, exit 0. Entry 7.
fn: makeAdder (size_t: n) fn: (int: x) int
    fn: addN (int: x) int
        if: n > 4294967295U
            return: x + 100
        return: x + 1
    return: addN

addBig: makeAdder 4294967296U
addSmall: makeAdder 4294967295U
int: a (addBig: 1)
int: b (addSmall: 1)
int: ok 0
if: a = 101 && b = 2
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
